## Building co-occurrence Matrix (COmatrix)

`table()` to build character-by-scene matrix

`crosprod()` for cross product to make symmetric character-by-character COmatrix

diagonal to zero removes self-occurances

```{r}
net_cmx <- crossprod(table(net_dat[1:2]))
diag(net_cmx) <- 0
net_df <- as.data.frame(net_cmx)
```

## Build Node Attribute Table

```{r}
#create dataset, rename 2 headings, summarize by number of occ.
vi <- net_dat |>
  dplyr::rename(node = "person", n = "occurrences") |>
  dplyr::group_by(node) |>
  dplyr::summarize(n = sum(n))

#types for future type organization
mon <- c("ABRAM", "BALTHASAR", "BENVOLIO", "LADY MONTAGUE", "MONTAGUE", "ROMEO")
cap <- c("CAPULET", "CAPULET'S COUSIN", "FIRST SERVANT", "GREGORY", "JULIET",
         "LADY CAPULET", "NURSE", "PETER", "SAMPSON", "TYBALT")

#Add Type column with succinct logic check to sort by
vi <- vi |>
  dplyr::mutate(type = dplyr::case_when(
    node %in% mon ~ "Montague",
    node %in% cap ~ "Capulet",
    TRUE          ~ "Other"
  ))
```

## Build Edge List

```{r}
# Make COmatrix into longform(+rows,-col), add 'from' col, change header name, remove entries with n=0
ed <- net_df |>
  dplyr::mutate(from = rownames(net_df)) |>
  tidyr::pivot_longer(
    cols      = -from,
    names_to  = "to",
    values_to = "n"
  ) |>
  dplyr::filter(n > 0)
```

