# Network Visualization

`quanteda. textplots::textplot_network()` can generate a network plot from a feature co-occurance matrix (FCM), but has limited customization vs `ggraph` . Convert data frame to document-feature matrix (DFM), then to an FCM

```{r}
net_dfm <- quanteda::as.dfm(net_df)
net_fcm <- quanteda::fcm(net_dfm, tri = FALSE)
```

```{r}
#generate network plot (initial)
tenMinFreq <- quanteda.textplots::textplot_network(
  x             = net_fcm,
  min_freq      = 0.1,
  edge_alpha    = 0.5,
  edge_color    = "gray50",
  edge_size     = 2,
  vertex_labelsize = net_dfm |>
    quanteda::convert(to = "data.frame") |>
    dplyr::select(-doc_id) |>
    rowSums() |>
    log(),
  vertex_color  = "#8b05a3",
  vertex_size   = 2
)
#changed min_freq to see if it would pick up any new values, A: Yes, why assume 0.5? I think weirdness is from density probability being greater than 1? 0.01 has all vertices connected. 0.5 could be to be consistant with quanteda documentation
